  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "IF evaluates only the selected branch, rejects numeric strings in its test, and turns omitted branches into 0 or FALSE",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, IF(logical_test, value_if_true, [value_if_false]) evaluates logical_test first through logical coercion (accepting numbers, logicals, and \"TRUE\" or \"FALSE\", while rejecting \"1\", \"\", and \"x\" with #VALUE!) and evaluates only the chosen branch, so an unchosen branch containing 1/0 does not raise #DIV/0!. An omitted selected branch returns 0, whereas a FALSE test with no third argument returns FALSE.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Recorded in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 across the cfunc_m1_2 oracle capture (mixed_operands rows 112-123 and error_order rows 76-79) and matched across 4,189 of 4,189 full-bank IF witness rows.",
